{
 "netpack": 1,
 "name": "diagonal_boulevard",
 "version": "0.2.0",
 "author": "netmod (task diagbv)",
 "description": "Diagonal boulevards: draw three diagonal roads joined side by side (each one cell over: along x on the down-right diagonal, one cell up on the other) and sc3netmod's DBV block makes them one 3-wide boulevard, the straight boulevard's cross-section turned 45 degrees: the outer roads are the carriageways, the middle one gives each an extra lane and holds a grass median with avenue 11204's trees. Straight single roads crossing it, meeting it from one side or closing its end get junctions with crosswalks; it narrows into the diagonal avenue or tapers into one of its three roads, closes with a round curb where all three stop, and turns into the straight boulevard where its drags go on straight. Lane lines are white dashes. Built by `diagbv.py build .` in this folder before install (art/ is made from the game's frames and is not shipped). Needs sc3netmod.dll with the DBV block. Traffic (task bvlanes): 3 lanes each way, right-hand, one way per side, every turn at the junctions; own lane specs (bvl_*.lanes.json, dbvlanes.py / bvlanes.py).",
 "game": {
  "Apps/SIMNTWRK.DLL": "693f65724a08f1bbc920c4ede1b6c1d5c78c8b95fce0164da10b03fbfe526f61"
 },
